SUIT SHIFT 2.1.2 — frame clearance

Base: the v2.1.1 source ZIP delivered in this conversation, NOT the older
v2.1.0 files currently on this GitHub branch. This patch is saved for version
control; it does not modify the hosted game by itself. The separately delivered
v2.1.2 HTML/ZIP contains the working update.

Apply inside the v2.1.1 game source directory with git apply, then npm run build.
The rail and cloth extend 8 CSS px outwards. Grid coordinates, card dimensions,
game logic, settings and level data remain unchanged. Adjacent labels move a
few pixels to maintain clearance. Local Chromium checks passed at 320x568,
360x640, 390x844, 430x932, 768x1024 and 1440x1000, including selected cards,
pointer swipe/undo, and direction-button mode. 15 Node tests passed.
No physical-device, hosted-page or offline lifecycle validation was performed.

